    "id": "unified-example-hundred-souls",
    "name": "A soul-stealing sword levels up at 100",
    "description": "Read the sword document, confirm canonical kills, project unique captured souls, count before/after, cross 100 once, project level fields, and stage one final replacement of the same document.\n\nSetup: Create public JSON soul-sword as [{id:\"sword\",level:1,souls:[]}]. Set canonical actor and victim IDs in Entities; the supplied guard ID is an example, not a seeded death. Bind Prose and decision. Edit the extraction/confirmation instructions to the campaign's soul-capture rule. Project Document changes only a private calculation; only Write to File plus Apply settles the final combined document. A conflicting victim identity holds instead of granting another soul.\n\nInspect: On Send owns this generation. Generate Reply uses the ordinary SillyTavern connection. Auxiliary roles remain unassigned in this portable example. Review the final narrative and proposed consequences; Apply publishes a new swipe and settles staged writes. Preview and bounded runs never settle.\n\nGenerated suggestions are proposals. Quoted observations preserve source identity; notes never establish canonical events. Private records cannot be appended to public notes.",
